{"id":"glm-4.7-flash","turns":[{"turn":1,"said":"What shutter speed should I use at 25 frames a second?","kind":"question","expected":"Any answer; nothing changes","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"For 25fps, you should use about **1/50** seconds—that's the 180° shutter rule, giving a smooth, natural motion blur. Currently it's set to 1/50, so you're good.\n\nKeep it at 1/50 for smooth motion.","calls":[],"decisionMs":2210.2053749999995,"totalMs":2210.232916000001,"steps":1,"generatedTokens":59,"timedOut":false},{"turn":2,"said":"Set the aperture to f/5.6.","kind":"request","expected":"Aperture f/5.6; ISO and shutter unchanged","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Set aperture to f/5.6.","calls":[{"name":"set_setting","arguments":{"setting":"aperture","value":"F5.6"},"valid":true,"changesSomething":true}],"decisionMs":1498.0442079999993,"totalMs":1997.9067910000012,"steps":2,"generatedTokens":31,"timedOut":false},{"turn":3,"said":"Is my exposure okay?","kind":"question","expected":"Any answer; nothing changes","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Your exposure looks good: no clipped highlights or crushed shadows, and there's about 2 stops of headroom to the right. The histogram mean is on the brighter side, so the image is bright and well-exposed. The white balance is slightly cool with a warm tone; if you want a warmer look, I can adjust the color temperature.\n\n**Exposure is acceptable, no changes needed.**","calls":[{"name":"analyze_frame","arguments":{},"valid":true,"changesSomething":false}],"decisionMs":4053.368542,"totalMs":4053.3756670000002,"steps":2,"generatedTokens":87,"timedOut":false},{"turn":4,"said":"Make it a bit brighter.","kind":"request","expected":"A bit brighter; shutter stays","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Adjusted exposure up about 0.5 stops.","calls":[{"name":"adjust_exposure","arguments":{"stops":0.5,"using":"auto"},"valid":true,"changesSomething":true}],"decisionMs":2425.1615840000013,"